{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2201","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Rigged Bracket Sequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A regular bracket sequence is a sequence consisting of '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', which can be turned into a valid math expression by inserting $$$1$$$ and $$$+$$$ any number of times into the sequence. For example, the sequence \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()(()())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is a regular bracket sequence, while \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"())(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are not regular bracket sequences."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a regular bracket sequence $$$S$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us consider shifting a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ to the right. Formally, when a subsequence $$$S_{i_1} S_{i_2} \\ldots S_{i_k}$$$ is shifted to the right, the characters on the chosen indices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"simultaneously"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" get reassigned as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_{i_1} \\leftarrow S_{i_k}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_{i_2} \\leftarrow S_{i_1}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_{i_3} \\leftarrow S_{i_2}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\ldots$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_{i_k} \\leftarrow S_{i_{k-1}}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In other words, the element of the $$$j$$$-th chosen index gets reassigned to the $$$((j-2) \\bmod k + 1)$$$-th chosen character."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, when $$$S$$$ is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()(()())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", shifting the subsequence $$$S_2 S_4$$$ changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". On the other hand, shifting $$$S_2 S_3 S_5$$$ changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"))"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please count how many "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-empty subsequences"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" make $$$S$$$ remain regular when shifted to the right. As the answer may be huge, you are only asked to output the answer modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$A sequence $$$a$$$ is a subsequence of a sequence $$$b$$$ if $$$a$$$ can be obtained from $$$b$$$ by the deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) element from arbitrary positions. Two subsequences are considered different if the sets of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positions"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the deleted elements are different. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 300\\,000$$$, $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"is even"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"regular"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" bracket sequence $$$S$$$ of length $$$n$$$ given as a string without spaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$300\\,000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output the answer modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$ on a separate line."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n2\n()\n4\n()()\n6\n(()())\n10\n()((())())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n8\n28\n312\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second test case, the $$$8$$$ non-empty subsequences that make $$$S$$$ remain regular when shifted to the right are as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_1$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_2$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_3$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_4$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_1 S_3$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_2 S_3$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_2 S_4$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$S_1 S_2 S_3$$$: changes $$$S$$$ to \""},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2201C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2201/problem/C"}